---
/**
 * TestLevels — the pyramid re-drawn as the argument it is meant to be: what
 * question each level can answer, what it costs to run, and what makes it fail
 * for a reason unrelated to the product.
 *
 * The bar is the share of the suite that shape implies, not a rule inherited
 * from somewhere else.
 */

const levels = [
  {
    name: 'Unit',
    share: 100,
    question: 'Does this function compute the right answer?',
    cost: 'microseconds',
    breaks: 'Nothing outside the function. It also proves nothing about the wiring.',
  },
  {
    name: 'API and contract',
    share: 64,
    question: 'Does this service honour what it promised?',
    cost: 'milliseconds',
    breaks: 'A schema change, a migration — the things you want to hear about.',
  },
  {
    name: 'Journey',
    share: 22,
    question: 'Can a person actually complete this?',
    cost: 'seconds',
    breaks: 'A layout change, a slow environment, a shared record. Often not the product.',
  },
];
---

<figure class="lu-figure levels">
  <div class="lu-figure__frame">
    <p class="heads">
      <span>Level, and its share of the suite</span>
      <span>The question it can answer</span>
      <span>What makes it fail</span>
    </p>

    <ul class="rows">
      {
        levels.map((level) => (
          <li class="row">
            <div class="head">
              <span class="name">{level.name}</span>
              <span class="bar" style={`--share:${level.share}%`} />
              <span class="cost">{level.cost}</span>
            </div>
            <p class="question">{level.question}</p>
            <p class="breaks">{level.breaks}</p>
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ul>
  </div>
  <figcaption class="lu-figure__caption">
    Step 1. The shape follows from cost and from the question each level can
    answer — so asking a browser journey to prove arithmetic is the most common
    waste in a real suite.
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  .rows {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
  }

  .row {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(12rem, 0.9fr) 1.1fr 1.1fr;
    gap: 0.5rem 1.25rem;
    align-items: start;
    padding: 0.875rem 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--sl-color-hairline);
  }

  .heads {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(12rem, 0.9fr) 1.1fr 1.1fr;
    gap: 1.25rem;
    margin: 0 0 0.5rem;
    font-family: var(--sl-font-mono);
    font-size: 0.6875rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    color: var(--sl-color-gray-4);
  }

  .row:first-child {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--sl-color-hairline);
  }

  .head {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.375rem;
  }

  .name {
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    font-weight: 590;
    color: var(--sl-color-white);
  }

  .bar {
    display: block;
    width: var(--share);
    height: 6px;
    border-radius: var(--lu-radius-pill);
    background: var(--sl-color-gray-5);
  }

  .cost {
    font-family: var(--sl-font-mono);
    font-size: 0.6875rem;
    color: var(--sl-color-gray-4);
  }

  .question {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    line-height: 1.45;
    color: var(--sl-color-gray-2);
  }

  .breaks {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    line-height: 1.45;
    color: var(--sl-color-gray-3);
  }

  @media (max-width: 44rem) {
    .heads {
      display: none;
    }

    .row {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 0.375rem;
    }
  }
</style>
